==English==

===Etymology===
From a moment on the TV series ''[[w:Happy Days|Happy Days]]'' in which the character Fonzie jumped over a shark on waterskis

===Verb phrase===
{{rfc-xphrase|Verb phrase}}
'''jump the shark'''

# {{idiom}} For something, often a television show, to have a significant storyline development whose ridiculousness or incredibility signifies that the series has lost its previous quality.
#: ''Happy Days '''jumped the shark''' when Fonzie jumped over a shark on waterskis.''

